100,20],[32761,26.0,1952,59,105,21]],"links":[["Mineral County in the Farmland Atlas","/farmland-atlas/montana/mineral-county"],["ARC or PLC in Mineral County","/arc-plc/montana/mineral-county"],["PRF calculator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, August to September came in under 90% of normal in 39 of 75 years on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 15 grids, the most of any pair, while April to May did it in 28. In 2025 the middle saw May to June at 54% of normal and November to December at 158%. For grid 31862 the preliminary estimate for July to August 2026 is 33.6, a NOAA figure that RMA&rsquo;s final index can differ from. Grid 32459 had its driest year in 1952 at 58%.</p>"}
